  "description": "*“Celia. You probably don’t know. That I’m this kind of person.”\n\n“Oh, if only Robert would tie me up like that.”*\n\nOn the surface, the Marquess and Marchioness of Dalton, Celia and Robert, seem perfect. But no one knows the truth behind the scenes. It’s already been two years since their marriage. Who could ever imagine that the two of them haven’t even properly consummated their marriage? They have their own reasons for avoiding each other in bed every night. What are the preferences they must hide from one another?\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
